        "summary": "Dc χT of the Tb9 analogue is close to nine non-interacting Tb(III) ions at room temperature, remains roughly constant to 100 K, then decreases on cooling, consistent with weak antiferromagnetic interactions, Stark depopulation and/or anisotropy. No ac signal (2–10 K, 3 Oe, 1–1500 Hz), so the complex is not an SMM.",
